{"diagnosis": "Fetch test uses 256 32-bit NOPs (mem_rdata_latched[1:0]==2'b11) expecting compressed_instr==0 and 4-byte advance with no trap. Excerpt defaults compressed_instr<=1 at line 892 and re-asserts <=1 at line 894, so 32-bit instructions are misclassified as compressed. This causes 2-byte stepping, misaligned fetches, and TRAP: cpu trap asserted / FAIL 0xdead.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -889,7 +889,7 @@
 			if (mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0001011 && mem_rdata_latched[31:25] == 7'b0000010 && ENABLE_IRQ)
 				decoded_rs1 <= ENABLE_IRQ_QREGS ? irqregs_offset : 3; // instr_retirq

-			compressed_instr <= 1;
+			compressed_instr <= 0;
 			if (COMPRESSED_ISA && mem_rdata_latched[1:0] != 2'b11) begin
 				compressed_instr <= 1;
 				decoded_rd <= 0;", "expected": "tohost PASS with no TRAP: cpu trap asserted, fetch alignment and progress check completes"}

